{
  "_comment": [
    "Bounding boxes for cities the builder ships as presets, in",
    "[west, south, east, north] degrees (EPSG:4326).",
    "",
    "These are hand-chosen urban-core boxes, not administrative boundaries.",
    "The point is a study area of roughly the size of the original Guwahati",
    "extent (~0.09 x 0.07 degrees, ~72 km2) so the cell counts, the runtime",
    "and the dashboard payload all stay in the same range.",
    "",
    "Anything not listed here still works: pass --bbox W S E N --name/--slug.",
    "",
    "Phoenix is deliberately included and deliberately outside India. The cost",
    "model in shared/constants.json is Indian municipal rupees per square",
    "metre; it does not transfer. The builder marks any city whose",
    "cost_basis_applies is false, and the dashboard shows the warning. It is a",
    "worked example of the assumption breaking, not an oversight."
  ],
